WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.440
A little meditation, plenty of Mai Tais--&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.520
Bruce Banner's recovery during the&nbsp;
Blip was nothing short of incredible.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.240
Marvel Studios' Phase 4 slate has&nbsp;
focused on new characters and new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.400
worlds in the Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;
for the current era of the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.800
officially titled "The Multiverse Saga,"&nbsp;
and the "She-Hulk" series adds Jennifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.480
Walters to the roster. In the comics, she's a&nbsp;
high-flying lawyer who gets a blood transfusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.680
from her cousin Bruce Banner after she gets&nbsp;
shot by mobsters in "Savage She-Hulk" #1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:38.320
But the Gamma radiation in his blood transforms&nbsp;
Jen into She-Hulk. Who could've seen that coming?

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:43.920
Thankfully, the series takes a different approach&nbsp;
to Jen's origin, as Bruce's blood spills into her&nbsp;

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.560
wound when the cousins get involved in a car&nbsp;
accident in the first episode of "She-Hulk."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.400
This makes sense because Banner would&nbsp;
know about the dangers of purposefully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:57.120
giving his cousin a blood transfusion&nbsp;
considering his own unique condition.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.640
The show also pulls from John Byrne's "The&nbsp;
Sensational She-Hulk" comics, which see the hero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.920
break the fourth wall to talk to the reader. Head&nbsp;
writer Jessica Gao told The Hollywood Reporter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.200
that she originally wanted to use that format&nbsp;
in an even bigger way in the series. She said,

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.800
"It was tricky finding the balance because if&nbsp;
I had my way, she'd be breaking the fourth wall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.880
every other sentence. Everybody had to&nbsp;
pull me back a little bit more from it."

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.200
Jennifer breaking the fourth wall injects&nbsp;
the series with a sense of fun, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.560
opposite Ruffalo's Professor Hulk, who teaches&nbsp;
his cousin how to handle her newfound abilities.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.231
"If you want to go back to your life&nbsp;
as a lawyer, I, I respect that."

00:01:38.661 --> 00:01:41.040
"Thanks…He doesn't mean that."

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.240
But while Jen and Bruce catch up, the&nbsp;
scientist reveals what the Hulk did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.480
during the Blip after Thanos erased&nbsp;
half of all life in the universe.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.760
The world drastically changed in the five years&nbsp;
between "Avengers: Infinity War" and "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:01.360
Endgame" due to half the population disappearing&nbsp;
as a result of the Snap. But when fans see Hulk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:06.960
again in "Endgame," Bruce Banner has figured out&nbsp;
a way to combine his alter-ego's strength and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:12.720
size next to his own intellect and personality.&nbsp;
It's a surprising development for the scientist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.800
but it's one that allows him to still be&nbsp;
part of the action while also pushing his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.960
character arc further. But "She-Hulk" Episode 1&nbsp;
reveals that it wasn't an easy feat to pull off.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.000
Bruce tells Jennifer that he&nbsp;
spent much of his time alone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.760
in his remote Mexican laboratory&nbsp;
which was funded by Tony Stark.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:36.000
"But this is where I spent the Blip fixing myself&nbsp;
and integrating the Hulk/Banner identities."

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.680
Bruce created a device there to&nbsp;
help him control his two sides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.880
putting the brains and the brawn together. This&nbsp;
lab would also be where Bruce healed his arm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:50.080
after the events of "Endgame," as he was&nbsp;
fairly injured from using the Stark Gauntlet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.280
It's great that Banner spent his&nbsp;
time productively during the Blip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:57.280
but it's hard not to think that he&nbsp;
could've been doing more out in the world.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:01.920
Bruce could have helped Natasha Romanoff&nbsp;
try and keep the world from falling apart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:07.013
with the remaining Avengers during the Blip. She's&nbsp;
not doing so great at the start of "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.013 --> 00:03:11.200
Endgame" because of everything she's been&nbsp;
through, and Bruce could have been there for her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.480
After all, once upon a time, the two&nbsp;
were very close in "Age of Ultron."

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.640
In the first act of "Avengers: Endgame,"&nbsp;
most of the surviving heroes work together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:26.080
during the fallout. Nebula, Rocket,&nbsp;
Okoye, Captain Marvel, and War Machine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.960
are all doing their part across Earth and&nbsp;
the universe. The fact that Bruce hid out in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:37.280
Mexico trying to work on his new Smart Hulk ego&nbsp;
and not helping his friends is quite unusual.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:41.440
Regardless of his absence during the blip,&nbsp;
it's safe to say that if Professor Hulk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.680
had not come to be, Jessica Walter's&nbsp;
transition into She-Hulk would have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.000
much harder to handle, or might&nbsp;
not have even happened at all.

